    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0636" n="538" xml:id="pg538"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cridler to Mr.
                            Hollis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of a letter<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d649-f1"/> from Mr. R. W. Geldart, complaining that the steamship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Beatrice</hi>, upon which he had a consignment of
                    beer and lard for a firm at Lourenco Marquez, discharged all of its Delagoa Bay
                    cargo into lighters at East London, under orders of the British Government. You
                    will please investigate the matter and report thereon to the Department. You
                    should use all proper efforts to protect the rights of the shippers.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. W. Cridler</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Third Assistant Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d649-f1" n="1" xml:id="d649-f1-content">
                <p>(Inclosure:) From R. W. Geldart, December 15, 1899, printed ante.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
